\title{tulpaGPU: CUDA Backend for the 'tulpa' Bayesian Engine}
\description{
Runs the device operations of the 'tulpa' engine on an NVIDIA graphics processing unit: dense and sparse Cholesky factorizations, factorizations batched across the cells of a nested Laplace grid, basis products, observation scatter and fused likelihood kernels. The CUDA driver and the 'cuSOLVER', 'cuBLAS', 'NVRTC' and 'cuDSS' libraries are loaded at run time, so installing the package needs only a C++ compiler. Once loaded, 'tulpa' sends each operation to the device when it lies above its measured size crossover, or always under control$device = "cuda".
}
